   "t": 70.03,
   "kind": "thought",
   "data": {
    "text": "In `lagos-lekki-v2` for a `120 mm / 3 h` storm over the whole area, defaults for pattern:\n\n### Baseline\n\nRun `r_19bad5451b9f8e42` - `120mm/3h`, no interventions:\n\n* whole area: `road_km_impassable` 384.7 km, `buildings_flooded` 29137, `max_depth_m` 2.051 m\n* inside `Lekki-Epe Expressway`:\n  * `area:Lekki-Epe Expressway:road_km_impassable` 34.912 km\n  * `area:Lekki-Epe Expressway:max_depth_m` 1.142 m\n  * `area:Lekki-Epe Expressway:flooded_area_km2` 0.7805 km2\n\nPassability threshold is 0.3 m. Expressway is impassable over ~35 km.\n\nScreening with `surrogate_sweep` for `road_km_impassable` pointed to city-wide new drainage as lowest effort. Surrogate numbers are predictions only and not cited. Confirmed by solver, one change at a time:\n\n### 1. Upgrade existing drains +40% city-wide\n\nRun `r_d0b5052b089ea53c`: `drain_upgrade capacity_factor 1.4` with no place = whole study area.\n\n* `area:Lekki-Epe Expressway:road_km_impassable` 34.513 km\n* `area:Lekki-Epe Expressway:max_depth_m` 1.129 m\n\nvs baseline: essentially no change. Not enough to keep Expressway passable.\n\n### 2. City-wide new drainage 40 mm/h\n\nRun `r_092b964bc62b8514`: `drain_upgrade add_mm_h 40.0` with no place = city-wide new drainage, never a local fix.\n\n* `area:Lekki-Epe Expressway:road_km_impassable` 1.091 km\n* `area:Lekki-Epe Expressway:max_depth_m` 0.405 m\n* `area:Lekki-Epe Expressway:flooded_area_km2` 0.1274 km2\n* `area:Lekki-Epe Expressway:people_exposed` 615 vs 3840 baseline\n\nWhole area delta alt - base `r_092b964bc62b8514 - r_19bad5451b9f8e42`:\n`road_km_impassable` -369.536 km, `buildings_flooded` -19030, `buildings_flooded_severe` -8206, `flooded_area_km2` -18.7568\n\nSingle intervention, ~97% reduction on Expressway impassable length, but still 1.09 km > 0, so not fully passable.\n\n### 3. City-wide 2x existing + 40 mm/h new\n\nRun `r_e561d6847c2ba564`: `drain_upgrade capacity_factor 2.0 + add_mm_h 40.0` whole study area.\n\n* `area:Lekki-Epe Expressway:road_km_impassable` 0.617 km\n* `area:Lekki-Epe Expressway:max_depth_m` 0.405 m\n* `area:Lekki-Epe Expressway:flooded_area_km2` 0.1 km2\n\nWhole area delta `r_e561d6847c2ba564 - r_19bad5451b9f8e42`:\n`road_km_impassable` -370.495 km, `buildings_flooded` -19227, `people_exposed` -73480\n\nBest tested, but still 0.617 km impassable.\n\n### Answer on smallest set for passable = 0 km impassable\n\nNo set tested achieves 0 km on the Expressway:\n\n* +40% existing alone: 34.513 km remains\n* city-wide new 40 mm/h alone: 1.091 km remains\n* city-wide 2x + 40 mm/h new: 0.617 km remains\n\nSmallest / most efficient large gain is the single intervention city-wide new drainage `40 mm/h` in `r_092b964bc62b8514`. Adding 2x existing capacity only saves an extra ~0.47 km on the Expressway.\n\nTo reach strict 0 km will need more than tested here - e.g. higher `add_mm_h`, localized drainage along the Expressway corridor, pond on open land, green - to be confirmed with new solver runs. 4-run budget used. Model is planning model, not forecast.\n"
   }
